      "side": 1,
      "message": "This changes the semantics of the original struct. The `uint rand[0]` as the only item is a \"trick\" that takes advantage of the fact that the first item in a struct has the same address as the struct itself (in pseudocode: `addressof(struct ec_response_rand_num)) \u003d\u003d `addressof(ec_response_rand_num.rand)`).\n\n`rand[0]` doesn\u0027t actually provide any memory to hold the contents, so when this is used, we [use allocated memory](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/util/ectool.c;l\u003d1554;drc\u003dfa9398743f429539cbd2d987790bb2af4a9e6517).\n\nIf we change it to `rand[1]`, it looks like it\u0027s supposed to be an array of size 1 (i.e., there is memory already allocated and no allocation is needed).\n\nInstead, I think you can make the `BUILD_ASSERT` size conditional on C++ vs C.",
